{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "readmission-by-condition",
  "title": "Readmissions by condition",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "3efc6a72-843f-442c-968f-576945fa747a",
      "question": "Compare the 30-day readmission rate for inpatient discharges with heart failure as the primary diagnosis, discharges with COPD as the primary diagnosis and all other inpatient discharges from April 2025 through August 2026. Leave out deaths and hospice discharges.",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-04T05:33:01.424397Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-04T05:33:10.676998Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**30-Day Readmission Rates by Primary Diagnosis Cohort (April 2025 – August 2026)**\n*Excluding deaths and hospice discharges*\n\n| Cohort | Index Discharges | 30-Day Readmissions | Readmission Rate |\n|--------|-----------------|---------------------|------------------|\n| Heart Failure | 191 | 40 | 20.94% |\n| COPD | 71 | 17 | 23.94% |\n| Other | 462 | 49 | 10.61% |\n\n**Key findings:**\n- **COPD** has the highest 30-day readmission rate at **23.94%** (17 of 71 discharges)\n- **Heart Failure** follows at **20.94%** (40 of 191 discharges)\n- **All other diagnoses** combined have a much lower rate of **10.61%** (49 of 462 discharges)\n\nThe analysis covers inpatient discharges from April 1, 2025 through August 31, 2026, using primary ICD-10 codes I50.x for heart failure and J44.x for COPD. Discharges with disposition \"expired\" or \"hospice\" were excluded as index events. [1]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Structured retrieval result — healthcare_clinical — evidence `hermes-receipt:a55cae598449e066ade7fab3b62b4e821d2d245bbd4374fe5d9a35d5fc81691a`",
